#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""
PINHOLE - minimal boolean-blind SQL injection extractor for MSSQL targets
behind an aggressive input-length filter that breaks sqlmap.

Why it exists:
  Some targets cap the length of an injectable parameter (app-level field
  validation, a Suhosin-style limit, a WAF). sqlmap's extraction payloads
  wrap every read in UNICODE(SUBSTRING((SELECT ...))) and a numeric
  bisection, which can run too long and 500 against such a cap. PINHOLE
  reads one bit per request with the shortest possible payload
  ( SUBSTRING(x,n,1)='c' ), so it slips under length filters that choke
  sqlmap.

Features:
  - minimal per-bit payloads (equality form, not UNICODE bisection)
  - per-character VERIFICATION: each matched char is re-confirmed and an
    unmatched position retried, to defeat flaky/noisy oracles
  - optional backend-affinity pinning (ARRAffinity) to stabilise the oracle
    on load-balanced targets
  - LIVE display with sqlmap-style output and result tables
  - CAP AWARENESS: --calibrate measures the payload budget; over-budget
    probes are reported as "unreachable" instead of returning junk
  - wordlist guessing for databases / tables / columns when catalog
    enumeration is blocked (non-DBA logins)
  - stores everything to SQLite

Mark the injection point in the raw request file with a single '*'.

For authorized security testing only. You are responsible for staying
within the scope of your engagement and the law.
"""

import argparse
import re
